// MR. MAS — Ep1 Act Four · the animatic v5: one layout per shot of timing lock v5 (INF-SHOTS5; the a4p5-lock pass).
// Lock v5 (data-v5.ts, generated by tools/lock_v5.py from the APPROVED stick timeline) plays the act as 83 shots. Every
// shot has a layout here, of one of three kinds (the verdicts are art-needs-v5 §3's, carried in the lock as sh.verdict):
//   R  reuse: THE EDITOR's v4 layout (shots4.ts) run through the `v4()` adapter, re-clocked on the v5 shot: its lines
//      (renamed back to the v4 ids the layout looks up, lock V4_IDS), its in-world texts and its story marks all come from
//      lock v5. Nothing in shots4.ts changes, so v4 stays renderable.
//   C  change: the v4 composition re-dressed with the v5 art (the art-v5 modules in shared/pixel: posts, the board's side
//      of the call, the letter, the pointer, the speakerphone, the hourglass insert, Terb's sheet...), re-built here where
//      the v4 layout could not take the new piece from outside.
//   N  new: a composition of the new v5 modules (Neleh's desk, the board head, the board screen, the unpacked bullpen...)
//      in the framing `art-v5/demos.ts` gives each one.
// A layout that throws, or a shot with no layout, draws the STICK FALLBACK (stickFallback: drawn stick figures on a plain
// set in the side's light, never a text label), is flagged in DRAW5_FAILED and reports `fallback` so the host's margin
// can mark it. Every layout carries `st` (what it is built from) and `standin` (it still holds a stand-in) for the margin
// and the shot list.
// Rules kept (studio/PIXEL_GUIDE.md, art-needs-v5 §5): native 480 x 270, master palette, whole-pixel moves, held drawings,
// nothing scaled but a screen's own pixels, no mirrored frames with lettering (S4.04 now uses Neleh's own right-shoulder
// drawing), Mas in the left third. The GLYPH dissolve stays at the Cancel click (S1.09 returns its layers); J1 is not
// drawn here: a host that plays J1 replaces frames t 1..59 after CANCEL_CLICK and ignores S1.09's layers there
// (art-v5/j1/pixel.ts j1PixelFrame; J1_PIXEL_OPTS keeps his tile's neon on the same guardrail clock).
// Mouths (INF-LIPSYNC5): every mouth comes from lipsync5.ts (mouth5 / roomMouth5 / boardMouths5 / silentMouth5, and
// v4Track5 for the adapter); the layouts here only pass them on in their `mouth:` fields. The lock's `face` decides who
// shows a mouth in a framing (art-needs-v5 §1.2), not the take's lip_sync flag: a line whose face is null draws 'rest'.
// `k` is shot-relative, `f` the v5 act frame; v4 layouts get the v4 act frame of the same shot position (f4 = v4 shot
// start + k) so their act-clocked loops and sequence clocks (the avalanche's S6 clock) run exactly as they did in v4.
